---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import HeaderBand from "../components/HeaderBand.astro";
import PageTitle from "../components/PageTitle.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About — Altair R."
  description="About Altair R., Senior Software Engineer and Head of Engineering at UNIVERSA AI."
  canonical="https://altairrostam.github.io/about/"
>
  <HeaderBand active="about" />

  <main class="content-main">
    <header class="page-header">
      <PageTitle title="About" icon="compass" />
    </header>

    <section class="about-body">
      <div class="about-text">
        <p>I'm Altair R. (full name Altair Rostam), a software engineer who tends to work across boundaries.</p>
        <p>I've built frontend applications, backend services, data pipelines, browser automation, cloud infrastructure, and AI systems. I started writing software professionally in 2019, and over time I've found that I care less about owning a particular layer of the stack than about understanding the problem well enough to make the whole thing work.</p>
        <p>These days I'm Head of Engineering at UNIVERSA AI, after joining as a Senior AI Engineer. The title changed; the way I work mostly didn't. I'm still hands-on, usually somewhere between a loosely defined idea and the production system it eventually has to become.</p>
        <p>I like problems with unclear edges: figuring out what actually needs to be built, finding the part everyone assumed somebody else owned, and getting systems from “this should work” to actually working.</p>
        <p>I write here about software engineering, AI, systems, work, and things I'm still figuring out.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="portrait">
        <img src="/assets/images/portrait.jpg" alt="Altair R.">
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="about-contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
      <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
      <p><code>altairrostam [at] gmail [dot] com</code></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
